Subject: Unsuspend windows of a workspace restored to a reconnected monitor

When a monitor disconnects, its workspace moves to another monitor as a
background workspace and its windows get xdg_toplevel SUSPENDED. When the
monitor reconnects, setupDefaultWS() moves the workspace back with
moveWorkspaceToMonitor(), which recomputes suspended states while the
workspace is not yet visible, and then makes it the active, visible
workspace by assignment without recomputing them. The later restore in
onConnect() calls changeWorkspace(), which returns early because the
workspace is already active. GTK 4 clients stop drawing while suspended,
so the window stays frozen until it is moved to another workspace.

Seen on asterix with a monitor that drops hot-plug when it wakes from
standby. Not checked against upstream main, which has rewritten this code.

Forwarded: no
---
diff --git a/src/output/Monitor.cpp b/src/output/Monitor.cpp
index 5b0e058..819ac82 100644
--- a/src/output/Monitor.cpp
+++ b/src/output/Monitor.cpp
@@ -1330,6 +1330,11 @@ void CMonitor::setupDefaultWS(const Config::CMonitorRule& monitorRule) {
     PNEWWORKSPACE->m_events.activeChanged.emit();
     PNEWWORKSPACE->m_visible     = true;
     PNEWWORKSPACE->m_lastMonitor = "";
+
+    // moveWorkspaceToMonitor above already recomputed suspended states, but
+    // before this workspace became the visible one, so a workspace moved back
+    // from another monitor keeps its windows suspended.
+    Desktop::globalWindowController()->updateSuspendedStates();
 }
 
